{
  // Declaration-only emit for the published package. The repo-root tsconfig
  // remains the solution-wide config used by `npm run typecheck`; this one
  // narrows to src and drops tests/stories so they stay out of `dist`.
  //
  // `paths` is CLEARED rather than inherited. The root config maps every
  // `@weasel-js/*` specifier to a sibling's `src/`, which is right for the
  // dev loop but wrong here: following core into source drags in core's own
  // bare aliases (`core/…`, `features/…`) that only core's tsconfig maps, and
  // it would inline core's declarations into ui's instead of referencing them.
  //
  // With no mappings, tsc resolves each sibling through the node_modules
  // workspace symlink and its `exports`/`types` — i.e. against core's BUILT
  // declarations, exactly as a consumer does. That is the whole payoff of
  // making these real packages, and it requires the dependency-ordered build
  // (siblings are built before ui; see the root `build` script).
  "extends": "../../tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "declaration": true,
    "emitDeclarationOnly": true,
    // Without this, a resolution mistake is silently destructive: tsc emits
    // even when it errors, so the first version of this config — which mapped
    // @weasel-js/core to core's SOURCE — pulled core's whole tree into the
    // program and scattered 1000+ .d.ts files across packages/core/src/,
    // which then broke core's own dts build. Fail before writing anything.
    "noEmitOnError": true,
    "declarationMap": true,
    // NOT incremental (the repo root turns it on; this overrides it). `vite
    // build` runs first with `emptyOutDir`, so it deletes the .d.ts files tsc
    // wrote last time — but tsc's incremental state still records them as
    // emitted, and plain `--incremental` checks input signatures, never
    // whether the outputs are still on disk. The second and every subsequent
    // build therefore emitted NOTHING and exited 0, and `@weasel-js/ui@0.5.0`
    // shipped an `exports` map pointing at .d.ts files that were not in the
    // tarball. CI never caught it because a cold checkout only ever builds
    // once. Keep this off: a bundler owns this outDir, so a tsc-side cache of
    // what's in it is always a lie waiting to happen.
    "incremental": false,
    "outDir": "./dist",
    "rootDir": "./src",
    "types": ["node"],
    "paths": {}
  },
  "include": ["src"],
  "exclude": [
    "node_modules",
    "dist",
    "**/*.test.ts",
    "**/*.test.tsx",
    "**/*.stories.ts",
    "**/*.stories.tsx",
    "**/__tests__/**"
  ]
}
